// SL-215 / design 275 U3 (codex r3 #1): an inline `try EXPR catch { … }` is
// normalized into the block form AT EVERY CHILD POSITION — the loop-exit
// regression beside K147's direct rows.
//
// K147 pins the inline catch where a statement holds it DIRECTLY and its
// subject suspends. This file is the same catch one wrapper down, with a SYNC
// subject: the enclosing loop spans a suspension (`yield_now()` beside the
// statement), the catch carries a `break`/`continue` for that loop, or a
// suspending call of its own, and the wrapper is every position the
// child-position funnel (`ast_walk.map_nodes`) names — a call argument
// (positional and labeled), a method-call argument, a receiver (field and
// method), a struct-literal field, a map-literal key and value, a tuple
// element, an array and a `Vector` literal element, an index, the place under a
// `&` argument, an interpolation operand, a `return` value, a `??` / `&&` / `||`
// operand, a nested inline catch inside a catch — plus the direct spelling as
// the control, and a value `if`/`match` arm that jumps, which is the same
// mechanism one construct over. Each cell is a `while` and a collection `for`,
// each with `break` and `continue`; the suspending catch is the `while` cell.
//
// TWO walks were the mechanism. `_inline_catch_rewrite` hand-rolled its visit
// and stopped at anything not an `ASTNode` — `Argument` is a plain dataclass,
// a struct-literal field and a map entry are TUPLES — so an inline catch inside
// `id(…)`, `Pair(a: …)`, `{k: …}` or `read(&a[…])` was never normalized, and a
// suspending call in its catch took the "pending SL-215" refusal. It rides
// `ast_walk.map_nodes` now. And the VALUE-CONDITIONAL lowering asked only
// "spans a suspension" of a leaf statement's conditional, so the normalized
// `try { } catch { break }` (and a value `if`/`match` whose arm jumps) sitting
// in a `let`, an argument or any other leaf position inside a spanning loop
// lowered IN PLACE with a raw jump: the `break` left the resume dispatcher and
// the driver re-entered it forever, the `continue` spun, and the code after the
// loop never ran — at every wrapper, exit 0 or a hang. `_vc_spans` asks the
// loop-exit clause too (`_has_loop_ctrl` under the loop that owns the jump), so
// the conditional takes the branch shape and the split routes the jump.
//
// THE ORACLE IS THE SYNC TWIN for every cell: `+ 100` after the loop is what a
// lost `break` skipped, and the cell values differ by kind (a `break` at the
// failing element, a `continue` past it, a suspending catch supplying its own
// value) so a jump that went to the wrong place reads as the wrong number.
//
// This body is a generated matrix: every cell is the same loop around one
// wrapper, and the sync twin is the driven cell minus the `yield_now()`.
// EXPECT: success
// EXPECT-OUTPUT:
// direct_break_while sync 101 driven 101
// direct_break_for sync 101 driven 101
// direct_continue_while sync 104 driven 104
// direct_continue_for sync 104 driven 104
// direct_suspend_while sync 107 driven 107
// call_arg_break_while sync 101 driven 101
// call_arg_break_for sync 101 driven 101
